  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0106) and found the likely cause. The drive is almost full, with only about 9 GB (3.5%) free out of 256 GB. Once free space drops under 10%, Windows slows down and updates can fail. Here's how to free up space:\n1. Empty the Recycle Bin and clear out your Downloads folder.\n2. Go to Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files and remove temporary files and old Windows Update files.\n3. Turn on OneDrive Files On-Demand (OneDrive settings > Sync and back up > Advanced settings). Your synced files then stay in the cloud until you open them.\n4. Uninstall any apps you no longer use.\n5. Do a full restart. Use Start > Power > Restart, because closing the lid doesn't restart it. Then install any pending Windows updates and restart again.\nIf it's still slow after that, open Task Manager (Ctrl+Shift+Esc) to see which app is using the most CPU or memory, and turn off apps you don't need in the Startup tab. If it's still slow after cleaning up, or you get blue screens or crashes, reply to this ticket and we'll look into it further. It would also help to know when you last restarted the laptop and whether the slowness started after an update or a new app install.",
  "internal_note": "User verified: Leo Martins (user_id 6, Sales), and BL-LT-0106 is assigned to him. Device check: online, Windows 11 Pro, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:52 UTC. Disk is 9.0 GB free of 256 GB (3.5%), with a low disk space warning. Severe low disk space is the likely cause of the slowness (KB-019 quick check 1, KB-017). Sent the user the KB-017 cleanup steps and the KB-019 restart, update and Task Manager steps. No queued actions. Next step: re-run the device status check to confirm free space is back above 10%. Per KB-017, escalate if it's still under 10% after cleanup (may need a larger drive or replacement). Per KB-019, escalate if it's still slow after cleanup and updates, or if there are blue screens or crashes. Still unknown: when the laptop was last restarted and whether the slowness started after an update or install.",
